    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d307">

                <pb facs="0529" n="1115" sameAs="frus:frus1949v07p2/pg1115"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890.00B/1–449: Circular airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Certain American
                        Missions </hi><anchor n="2" xml:id="d307-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-01-04T08:10:00-05:00">January 4,
                            1949—8:10 a. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Containment of Communism in Southeast Asia</hi>
                </p>
                <p>Embassy London states that the UK Foreign Office feels that because of political
                    differences it would be impossible to bring Asiatic and western nations together
                    at a conference to discuss the containment of Communism in southeast Asia. The
                    Foreign Office hopes to arrange continuing discussions through diplomatic
                    channels with all countries concerned.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d307-f1" n="2" type="source" xml:id="d307-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to 15 posts at Bangkok, Batavia, Canberra, Colombo, Hanoi, Karachi, Manila,
                    Moscow, Nanking, New Delhi, Paris, Rangoon, Saigon, Singapore, and The
                    Hague.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
